pps: clients: gpio: drop the capture-clear property read

Stable commit 0662b3dd0c61f ("pps-gpio: remove dead capture_clear code")
removes the capture_clear field and all code depending on it, as upstream never
sets it. Downstream rpi-6.12.y carries 5a44f901d948a ("added capture_clear
option to pps-gpio via dtoverlay (#2433)"), that sets it from the
capture-clear property. The stable commit merged without conflict, leaving
that assignment to a removed member.

Drop the property read, as Raspberry Pi's rpi-6.12.y does since 6.12.118.
The capture_clear parameter of the pps-gpio overlay no longer has an effect.

diff --git a/drivers/pps/clients/pps-gpio.c b/drivers/pps/clients/pps-gpio.c
index 0ac035f011fd5..96e169a35cedb 100644
--- a/drivers/pps/clients/pps-gpio.c
+++ b/drivers/pps/clients/pps-gpio.c
@@ -111,9 +111,6 @@ static int pps_gpio_setup(struct device *dev)
 	data->assert_falling_edge =
 		device_property_read_bool(dev, "assert-falling-edge");
 
-	data->capture_clear =
-		device_property_read_bool(dev, "capture-clear");
-
 	data->echo_pin = devm_gpiod_get_optional(dev, "echo", GPIOD_OUT_LOW);
 	if (IS_ERR(data->echo_pin))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(data->echo_pin),
